<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is a Turnover Certificate?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>A turnover certificate is a CA-certified document confirming total gross revenue (sales turnover or gross receipts) for a specific financial year, verified against ITR, GST returns, or audited financial statements. Authenticated with CA signature, seal, and UDIN. It certifies the top-line revenue &ndash; not profit, not net worth.</p>
                    <p>For companies: verified against audited P&amp;L Account. For proprietorships/partnerships: against ITR-3/ITR-4 and GST returns (GSTR-9). Can cover single year or multi-year (3/5 years) for tender requirements. Distinctly different from an audit report. For <a href="/statutory-audit/mumbai">Statutory Audit Mumbai</a>, see our page.</p>
                    <p>For Mumbai businesses in MCGM tenders, the certificate is the primary eligibility document. Tender specifies minimum turnover threshold &ndash; e.g., Rs 3 Cr average over 3 years. With UDIN, tender authority verifies authenticity online. For <a href="/gst-registration/mumbai">GST Registration Mumbai</a>, see our page.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Turnover Certificate:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Turnover:</strong> Total gross revenue from operations for a financial year</li>
                        <li><strong>UDIN:</strong> 18-digit ICAI code for online verification by tender authorities and banks</li>
                        <li><strong>GEM Portal:</strong> Government e-Marketplace requiring turnover proof for seller eligibility</li>
                        <li><strong>Prescribed Proforma:</strong> Tender-specific format &ndash; non-compliance causes bid rejection</li>
                        <li><strong>GSTR-9:</strong> GST annual return as source for GST-based turnover verification</li>
                        <li><strong>GST-ITR Reconciliation:</strong> Resolving differences between GST and ITR turnover</li>
                    </ul>

                </div>
            </div>
